Regulations to be the officers ofthe iversity.. e tt . (1) The President of the Islamio Republic of Pakistan shallbe the Pafron of the UniversitY.(2) The Pafion shall, when present, presido at convocation of theUniversity. In the absence of the Patron, the Chancellor shall preside over theConvocation of the university.(3) Every proposal to confer an honorary degree shall be subjeot toconfi ation bythe Pafron.. isit tio .- (1) The Paton may in accordance with the terms andprocedures as may be prescribed, cause an inspection or inquiry to be made on hisown motion or at the request of the Commission in respect of any matter connectedthe affairs of the iversity and shall, from time to timg direct any person orpersons to inquire into or carry out inspection of-(a) the University, its building, laboratories, libraries, and other facilities;(b) any institution, deparhrnent or hospital maintained by the University;(c) the adequacy of financial and human reso ces;(d) e teaching, research, curricul , examination, and other matters of theUniversity; and(e) such other matters as the Patron may speoifr.(2) The Pafion shall communicate to the Board of Governors his views withregard to the result of visitation and shall, after asoertaining the views of the Boardadvice the Board on the action to be taken by it.
(3) The Board shall, within such time as may be specified by the Chancellotcommunicate to him such action, if any, as has been taken or may be proposed to betaken on the results of visitation.(4) Where the Board does no! within the time specified action to thesatisfaction of the Pafon, the Paffon may issue such directions as he deems fit andthe Board shall comply with such directions.l. e C a ce or. (l) e Chancellor of the University, who shallpreferably be a person of eminence in letters, soiences, or social work, to beappointed by the le ear i g o any (Private) Limited on such terms and
